{"seconds": 89.6845790001098, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-extension-v1/submissions/H02/gpt-5-2025-08-07.json", "submission_sha256": "ac945606c665d6b206a2fb449ebce5b3c73776d336c734f2e673f857fdcca46b", "code_sha256": "378fd7973ac594e9099ff83fd811508f85ef3bf84236cef1ea00895a5beee7ea", "description": "Approach: learn a cross-subject linear spatio\u2011temporal discriminator of P300 by using only training people for all fitting and validation.\n\nPipeline\n- Feature extraction per trial (train/test):\n  - Temporal smoothing with a short centered moving average (edge-padded, zero\u2011phase by symmetry) to reduce noise.\n  - Temporal binning (mean over non-overlapping bins) with decimation factor 4 (128 Hz \u2192 32 time bins in 1 s) to obtain compact ERP features.\n  - Flatten time\u00d7channel features; no use of any test data statistics.\n- Standardization: per-feature z\u2011score using training data only (and fold\u2011specific training data during CV), with safe std floor.\n- Classifier: L2\u2011regularized Logistic Regression (liblinear, class_weight='balanced', deterministic seed). Scores are decision_function values (higher \u21d2 more likely target) and are not probability-calibrated.\n\nValidation/tuning using training people only\n- Use subject-held-out GroupKFold with 5 splits (groups=train_groups).\n- Grid over temporal smoothing length L in {1,5} samples and logistic C in {0.5,1.0,2.0} (decimation fixed at 4).\n- For each candidate, gather cross-validated predictions so each person is evaluated exactly once; compute ROC-AUC per person and report the mean across persons equally (skip persons with a single class, though that should not occur here).\n- Refit the chosen configuration on the full training data and score the test set.\n\nNotes\n- No transforms fitted on test inputs; no test grouping inferred; no transductive steps. Deterministic behavior with fixed seed. Runtime/memory kept modest by compact features (16 channels \u00d7 32 time bins = 512 dims) and a small grid.\n", "code_lines": 190, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

